  "title": "Bratu-2021-network-10.1016/j.cortex.2021.08.018",
  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from a single patient with drug-resistant epilepsy and a right posterior temporal periventricular nodular heterotopia (PVNH). High-frequency (43 Hz) stimulation of the PVNH elicited autoscopic hallucinations, and single-pulse electrical stimulation was used to map effective connectivity. The dataset supports multi-modal connectivity analysis (stimulation-evoked potentials, functional and structural connectivity) of the network underlying bodily self-consciousness disturbances. It includes iEEG recordings, contact coordinates and a defaced T1 image.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG was recorded at 4096 Hz from 128 channels (XLTek Quantum) with depth electrodes. Bipolar stimulation with a clinical stimulator used 43.3 Hz biphasic high-frequency trains (0.25-3 mA, 5 s) and single-pulse stimulation (20 pulses per trial, 15 s interval, 3 ms pulse duration). Original AnyWave ADES data were converted byte-for-byte to BrainVision format in iEEG-BIDS.",
